WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
- You guys practice something you call

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.690
stoke activism, right? What is that?

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.839
- Well, basically stoke activism.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:09.090
Our main mission is to bring bummer levels

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.727
down to a zero. We
believe. Yeah, we believe

00:00:12.727 --> 00:00:15.592
that if we can eradicate all bummer

00:00:15.592 --> 00:00:17.940
then world peace can be achieved.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:18.810
- Nicely said.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:19.643
- Yeah

00:00:19.643 --> 00:00:20.476
- Yeah

00:00:20.476 --> 00:00:22.890
- Yeah. And then someone
made us hip to the reality

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:25.230
that the government is
actually responsible

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:29.529
for a lot of city, state
and nationwide. Bummer.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:32.760
So yeah, we go into city council meetings

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.860
and just try to hold them accountable.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.560
- Okay. When was the
last time you were stoked

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.140
or when was the last time
you felt this kind of chill?

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.330
Cause I'm obsessed with
this kind of chill.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.360
- I'm so un bummed right now. Like

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.780
I am the most un bummed.
Just like your presence

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.310
is like un bumming me out.
So like. I'm so stoked

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.500
- I feel pretty good
about life right now too.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.210
Yeah. I did before you came in

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.130
but I definitely feel even better now.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.190
I feel like you have a really
good energy. I like it.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:02.098
- Thank you.

00:01:02.098 --> 00:01:03.810
- So wait, do you remember
the first time that

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.995
you decided to get politically active?

00:01:05.995 --> 00:01:06.903
- I do.

00:01:06.903 --> 00:01:10.528
I was nine years old. I
was in elementary school

00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:12.780
and the school was trying to do a

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.522
sign seating for lunch.
But I felt that was

00:01:15.522 --> 00:01:17.706
incredibly draconian
cause that was the only

00:01:17.706 --> 00:01:20.940
period of the day where
we had any sort of agency

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.500
in who we were kicking it with.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.379
So I came in one morning
and I chained myself

00:01:26.379 --> 00:01:30.101
to a lunch table and I sat there in the

00:01:30.101 --> 00:01:32.100
sweltering heat for nine hours

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.667
but I didn't sweat cause
I was cool with purpose.

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:40.667
- Cool with purpose. I love this

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.630
- So Margret what would you like

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.970
to see Chad and JT advocate for?

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.980
- I think that your whole, like, you know

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.320
just trying to stoke
it up, like just stoke

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.080
us all up and keep us from being bummed

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.620
is so inspiring. I think this
is really, really important.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.590
So I would just like you
to continue your work.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:01:59.423
- All right

00:01:59.423 --> 00:02:00.256
- Thank, Thank you.

00:02:00.256 --> 00:02:01.089
- Yes.

00:02:01.089 --> 00:02:01.922
- Thank you for the vote of confidence.

00:02:01.922 --> 00:02:02.755
- Yeah. Yes

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.860
- Yeah. I love you guys so much.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.930
So, wait, you guys have done some singing

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.493
